## Learning Center
- [When Should Organizations Use a Vulnerability Disclosure Program Instead of a Bug Bounty?](https://www.synack.com/learning-center/when-should-organizations-use-a-vulnerability-disclosure-program-instead-of-a-bug-bounty/)
- [What Are the Differences Between Penetration Testing and Bug Bounty Programs?](https://www.synack.com/learning-center/what-are-the-differences-between-penetration-testing-and-bug-bounty-programs/)
- [What Is a Vulnerability Disclosure Program?](https://www.synack.com/learning-center/what-is-a-vulnerability-disclosure-program/): A vulnerability disclosure program is a formal, governed process for receiving security vulnerability reports from external parties\. It defines scope, reporting channels, and legal protections, letting organizations handle unsolicited findings responsibly and integrate them into security operations\.
This article covers why organizations establish vulnerability disclosure programs, what they include, how disclosures are received and handled, what they are not designed to do, and how they fit alongside other security testing models\.

